{
  "id": "5-9-defender-4-lab-fly-and-fire",
  "title": "5.9.4 Lab: Fly and fire",
  "description": "The ship slides off the canvas and Space does nothing. Keep the ship on the canvas with two ifs, fire on a cooldown, and delete the shots that leave the top.",
  "type": "lesson",
  "estimateMins": 18,
  "category": "Unit 2: moSHion: Applied Game Development",
  "unit": "5.9 Project: Defender, Part A",
  "preview": "moshion",
  "week": 14,
  "slos": [
    "SLO-3"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "title": "Keep the ship on the canvas",
      "instructions": "Hold left for a while: the ship slides off the canvas. In `moveShip()`, after the two lines that move it, add two ifs that put it back: when `ship.x` is less than 20, set it to 20; when it is more than 380, set it to 380. The ship is 36 pixels wide and `x` is its centre, so 20 keeps all of it on the screen.",
      "hints": [
        "`if (ship.x < 20) ship.x = 20;`",
        "The second if is the same shape, with `>` and 380."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "title": "Fire on a cooldown",
      "instructions": "In `fire()`, first count `cooldown` down: take 1 off it while it is above 0. Then, when Space is held **and** `cooldown` is 0, build a shot: a 6 by 14 sprite at `(ship.x, ship.y - 18)` with `collider = 'none'` (so it passes through things, as in 5.2.17) and the colour `'yellow'`. Push it onto `bullets`, then set `cooldown` to 12 so the next shot has to wait 12 frames. Hold Space: the shots should come about five a second, evenly spaced.",
      "hints": [
        "`if (cooldown > 0) cooldown -= 1;` is the countdown, from 5.9.2. Leave out the `if` and `cooldown` runs on below 0, so `cooldown === 0` is never true again and the ship cannot fire.",
        "`if (kb.pressing('space') && cooldown === 0) { ... }` is the test, from 5.9.3. The sprite, the push and `cooldown = 12;` all go inside its braces."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "title": "Shots that leave are deleted",
      "instructions": "Every shot climbs 8 pixels a frame and never stops. In the loop in `moveBullets()`, a shot whose `y` is less than -20 has left the top: delete it and splice it out of `bullets`, as Flappy did with its pipes in 5.4.6. The loop runs from the end of the array to the start because a splice moves every later shot down one place; going backwards, none is skipped. Hold Space and watch 'shots alive' at the top: it should stay at 4 or fewer. If it keeps climbing, shots are not being removed.",
      "hints": [
        "`bullets[i].delete();` takes the shot off the screen and `bullets.splice(i, 1);` takes it out of the array. You need both.",
        "Both lines go inside `if (bullets[i].y < -20) { ... }`."
      ]
    }
  ],
